Modeling changes of the MQT-TZ TA (hot_cache_ta.c as published), applied before tools/ta2imp/ta2imp.py
translates it.  Everything the model leaves out or changes is here, as C; the [ta.broker] table of
mqttz.toml only says what to translate.

1. get_key: the model analyzes the storage path.  The key is looked up in secure storage under
   cli_id and saved there when it is missing; the in-memory key (key_mode == 0, keyinmem) and the
   copy of the id into my_id are left out, so key_mode goes from the signature and the two calls.
   res and save_key_res are declared here because the model's variable names are declared in
   MQTTZ-PROGRAM-DECL (env/base.maude) and ta2imp does not declare new ones.
2. read_raw_object: the model reads an object whole and has no buffer sizes, so there is no byte
   count to compare with the object size and no short-buffer case; the size parameters of
   read_raw_object and cipher_buffer go.  The sizes passed to the TEE API stay (the model does not
   read them).
3. payload_reencryption: decrypt with the origin key (TA_AES_MODE_DECODE) and encrypt with the
   destination key (TA_AES_MODE_ENCODE).  Upstream calls alloc_resources the other way round, with
   FIXME comments on both calls.
4. payload_reencryption takes the parts of its memory references (origin client id, IV and data,
   destination client id and data) as pointers.  TA_InvokeCommandEntryPoint, which the model
   replaces by its dispatcher (ta/main.imp), checks the parameter types, pre-loads the keys
   (fill_ss) and splits the references.
5. Output that the model does not have is left out: logging (printf, EMSG), the timing of the
   benchmark (TEE_GetSystemTime, TEE_TIME_SUB and the times written to params[2]), and the IV
   written back to params[1].  The IV of the encryption is the content of a fresh buffer instead of
   the copy of upstream's fixed fake_iv.
6. Memory: TEE_Malloc never fails in the model, so its checks go, and the model frees a buffer when
   the function that allocated it returns, so the TEE_Free calls go.
7. save_key: the handle starts as TEE_HANDLE_NULL (the model's TEE_CreatePersistentObject reads it),
   and the result of TEE_CloseAndDeletePersistentObject1 is kept in res.

